# 5c-5: Propose-and-confirm convention lifecycle

## Approach

Add three interlocking pieces to the convention system: (1) history tracking that records support/confidence snapshots across FCA rebuilds, (2) a lifecycle module that detects trend signals in the history and generates durable proposals, and (3) inverse checking that warns when new/modified code matches deprecated or forbidden conventions. The MCP tool `sutra_conventions` surfaces all of this — listing conventions with their state and pending proposals, and accepting/dismissing proposals.

The proposal system is strictly propose-and-confirm: sutra detects signals and proposes transitions, but the human accepts or dismisses. Dismissed proposals don't nag — they track the signal direction at dismissal time and only re-trigger if the signal reverses.

