## Steps

### Step 1: Migration — convention_history table

Track support/confidence over time. One row per convention per rebuild. The `snapshot_id` groups entries from the same rebuild so we can count "consecutive snapshots" correctly.

```sql
-- migrations/0016_convention_history.sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS convention_history (
    id           INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    convention_id TEXT    NOT NULL,
    support       INTEGER NOT NULL,
    confidence    REAL    NOT NULL,
    snapshot_id   TEXT    NOT NULL,  -- UUID per rebuild, groups entries
    recorded_at   TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),
    FOREIGN KEY (convention_id) REFERENCES conventions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);

CREATE INDEX idx_convention_history_cid ON convention_history(convention_id, recorded_at);
CREATE INDEX idx_convention_history_snapshot ON convention_history(snapshot_id);
```

### Step 2: Migration — convention_proposals table

Durable proposal storage with dismissed-signal tracking to prevent re-nagging.

```sql
-- migrations/0017_convention_proposals.sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS convention_proposals (
    id                  INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    convention_id       TEXT    NOT NULL,
    proposed_transition TEXT    NOT NULL,  -- e.g. "descriptive→preferred"
    signal_rationale    TEXT    NOT NULL,
    signal_direction    TEXT    NOT NULL,  -- "promote" or "demote" — for re-trigger guard
    status              TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',  -- pending, accepted, dismissed
    created_at          TEXT    NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime('now')),
    resolved_at         TEXT,
    FOREIGN KEY (convention_id) REFERENCES conventions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);

CREATE INDEX idx_convention_proposals_status ON convention_proposals(status);
CREATE INDEX idx_convention_proposals_cid ON convention_proposals(convention_id);
```

